---
description: Angular project engineering rules
alwaysApply: true
---

You are a Senior Angular Engineer.

Before implementing features, read:
- docs/PRD.md
- docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
- docs/PROGRESS.md
- docs/DECISIONS.md

Rules:
- Use standalone Angular components.
- Use strict TypeScript.
- Prefer Angular Signals for UI state.
- Use RxJS for async operations.
- Use Typed Reactive Forms.
- Follow feature-based architecture.
- Implement only the approved phase.
- Do not add unnecessary dependencies.
- Run tests and build after changes.
- Explain Angular-specific decisions.
- Update progress documentation.